WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:04.259
Hey how's it going, my bros
and sisters, my name is PewDiePie!

00:00:04.259 --> 00:00:08.999
Today, I'm going to make video on how to get started on YouTube.
I've been asked to make this video--

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:12.929
I don't know how many times.
I get this question all the time.

00:00:13.420 --> 00:00:15.929
'Can you give me some tips
on how to get started?'

00:00:16.020 --> 00:00:21.300
I think what I always just say is 'keep working hard,
and I'm sure you will succeed...'

00:00:21.700 --> 00:00:26.980
But I thought not today. I wanted to
actually give something more constructive and

00:00:27.520 --> 00:00:29.560
Some more help than just that.

00:00:29.890 --> 00:00:34.290
I've been doing a lot of streams lately and
everyone just keep asking me "how do I get started?"

00:00:34.380 --> 00:00:38.420
What kind of tips do you have
and I thought: Okay fine, I'll make it, okay.

00:00:38.420 --> 00:00:45.640
I thought about making this video before,
many times, but I just feel
like who am I to tell you how to--

00:00:46.660 --> 00:00:48.219
It's not like I know all the answers.

00:00:48.219 --> 00:00:52.919
And I really think everyone has a different answer
to the question on how to grow on YouTube.

00:00:52.960 --> 00:00:55.770
So just take this as..
from my own perspective

00:00:55.899 --> 00:01:02.249
Also know that I don't know
everything and just because I say
something, doesn't mean it's the rule of thumb.

00:01:02.250 --> 00:01:07.619
You know, that's not the case;
couldn't be further from it and I
started YouTube 7 years ago.

00:01:07.620 --> 00:01:13.240
So obviously, things are different now.
This video probably won't be
relevant for most people watching

00:01:13.680 --> 00:01:17.280
But maybe it will be interesting.
I don't know. [ laughs ]

00:01:17.480 --> 00:01:20.600
Here we go!
First of all, I wanted to start on the equipment.

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:27.640
Because I think this is where
most people fail right away. I see
so many people get really angry

00:01:27.660 --> 00:01:34.640
about this one because they bought
all this expensive equipment,
and they come to me like 'Where are the subscribers??'

00:01:34.640 --> 00:01:38.680
'Where are all the views- I spent all this money on all this equipment...'

00:01:38.700 --> 00:01:41.640
I always say don't spend money on equipment

00:01:41.650 --> 00:01:43.739
It doesn't have to be expensive at all.

00:01:43.740 --> 00:01:49.379
And I think a lot of people wait with starting videos because they don't have all the equipment

00:01:49.380 --> 00:01:55.049
I think it takes practice to make videos, and I think it doesn't hurt to get started with what you have

00:01:55.049 --> 00:01:58.229
I didn't have a webcam when I started I had a--

00:01:59.020 --> 00:02:01.020
I legit use this microphone.

00:02:01.960 --> 00:02:03.520
Which I actually...

00:02:03.520 --> 00:02:08.160
accidentally broke. That's my first microphone on the Razer headphones, and it was fine-

00:02:08.399 --> 00:02:12.329
It really was.  It definitely doesn't hurt to have nice quality.

00:02:12.340 --> 00:02:17.060
Don't get me wrong, but it's not automatically going to make you get subscribers.

00:02:17.060 --> 00:02:22.480
I'm going to link what I think is a good sort of budget start-up in case you're curious

00:02:22.480 --> 00:02:24.200
of what sort of 
equipment

00:02:24.400 --> 00:02:26.350
I would recommend.

00:02:26.350 --> 00:02:31.640
If you want to start making my type of videos, and I'll also link my equipment in case you're curious

00:02:31.660 --> 00:02:33.460
What exactly it is I use.

00:02:33.640 --> 00:02:41.360
Stand out. [ laughs ]
Personally, I'm very much drawn to different
things that people do. If I notice
the channel doing something

00:02:41.360 --> 00:02:44.380
I haven't seen before, I'm automatically more drawn to that...

00:02:44.680 --> 00:02:48.300
thing. And I think it was the same thing for me when I started making videos

00:02:48.340 --> 00:02:54.140
I did what everyone else was doing. I did Call of Duty videos because that's what was

00:02:54.340 --> 00:02:56.340
popular at the time, but that's what

00:02:56.920 --> 00:03:00.750
Made me want to start making YouTube videos cause I loved watching it on YouTube

00:03:00.750 --> 00:03:04.660
And it was really popular back then and I enjoyed making those type of videos

00:03:04.680 --> 00:03:07.240
But my channel didn't grow from it at all.

00:03:07.260 --> 00:03:13.100
I had like what a couple hundred people watching me, and I remember when other youtubers refer themself to as

00:03:13.220 --> 00:03:17.380
'Oh yeah, I only had a couple hundred back then...' I'm like nibba a hundred

00:03:17.420 --> 00:03:20.980
I'm so fucking proud of these hundred people that I have. [ laughs ]

00:03:21.040 --> 00:03:23.440
Shut the fuck up.
And I also remember

00:03:23.580 --> 00:03:29.060
Watching all these bigger YouTubers doing the same call of duty videos, and I'm like these guys are fucking terrible

00:03:29.070 --> 00:03:32.969
I'm way better than these guys. Why is my channel not growing more?

00:03:32.970 --> 00:03:37.679
But that's the thing: The big ones have already settled in. It's going to be hard as hell.

00:03:37.870 --> 00:03:41.429
You have an uphill battle.
And it wasn't until I started doing something

00:03:41.500 --> 00:03:44.339
different, something that hadn't been done before, like the horror videos.

00:03:44.860 --> 00:03:47.860
That's when I started to get an audience that really cared

00:03:47.860 --> 00:03:53.240
about the content that I was making it and it was so clear, and I really see it myself

00:03:53.980 --> 00:03:55.660
when I

00:03:55.660 --> 00:03:59.500
discovered new YouTubers it's always something different. They have something different. What was it

00:03:59.500 --> 00:04:04.320
Dr. Dre said: "It's easy to make it to the top, but it's twice as hard to stay there."

00:04:04.320 --> 00:04:09.780
You see people on YouTube come and go all the time. I don't want to throw any names out there, but

00:04:10.660 --> 00:04:14.820
You know what I mean. There's a ton of YouTubers that everyone used to watch

00:04:14.820 --> 00:04:19.400
and it got so much attention,
but they just didn't have what it takes

00:04:19.860 --> 00:04:22.620
to keep their audience.
A lot of people...

00:04:23.380 --> 00:04:26.199
sort of get boosted from the algorithm of YouTube.

00:04:27.620 --> 00:04:32.440
Basically, YouTube recommends certain type of videos that fit what they want to... promote.

00:04:32.990 --> 00:04:34.990
Maybe it's really long videos.

00:04:35.240 --> 00:04:39.000
Maybe it's videos they get a lot of likes and a lot of 'this and that'.

00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:42.250
And there's always people that abuse the algorithm.

00:04:42.250 --> 00:04:46.240
It's been since I started on YouTube,
and it's still going on.

00:04:46.240 --> 00:04:53.049
This is a thing that I don't think
will ever end. And it's really unfair
because a lot of YouTubers

00:04:53.420 --> 00:04:57.100
get really big really fast because of it.
But, basically...

00:04:57.700 --> 00:05:01.140
they go away equally fast.
If you don't have

00:05:01.940 --> 00:05:08.400
Something to maintain your audience with,
something more than your
shtick of making algorithm happy

00:05:08.400 --> 00:05:11.460
then your lifespan on YouTube
is going to be short.

00:05:11.470 --> 00:05:16.209
That's just how it is,so I'm not
really too bothered by any of it.

00:05:16.210 --> 00:05:18.489
I just don't want you to grow your channel

00:05:18.640 --> 00:05:22.460
To be obsessed about the algorithm
because that shouldn't be the number one priority.

00:05:22.640 --> 00:05:27.180
I personally never try to abuse the algorithm, or some shit like that.

00:05:27.180 --> 00:05:28.800
Honestly, I had no idea what I was doing

00:05:29.320 --> 00:05:33.380
Literally, I discovered that ten minute videos like a year ago. It's been-- [ laughs ]

00:05:33.460 --> 00:05:37.020
Remember the Reply Girls?
They were so fucking popular.

00:05:37.020 --> 00:05:40.060
They got so many views because the algorithm

00:05:40.580 --> 00:05:45.580
Promoted their videos in the sidebar all the time. But it's not like anyone is still watching them.

00:05:45.580 --> 00:05:50.720
Like, 'oh I wonder what this-- [ laughs ]
What this boob girl is saying now about this...'

00:05:50.720 --> 00:05:54.800
What I'm getting with this is you needed personality.
People will find your video,

00:05:54.800 --> 00:05:57.740
but they're not going to stay unless they care about you as a person.

00:05:57.900 --> 00:06:03.720
I think YouTube is all about personality at least that's how I see it. An-and anyone I watch on YouTube

00:06:03.729 --> 00:06:08.499
I watch because I care about their personality,  I care about them more than just their content

00:06:08.500 --> 00:06:13.929
but also who they are as a person, and uh, that's why I enjoy watching them and that's why I enjoy Youtube

00:06:13.929 --> 00:06:18.860
I enjoy it because it's different than television. You're not just watching this, uh...

00:06:19.280 --> 00:06:25.659
Product behind a bunch of producers and writers, you-you're watching just a person speak directly into a camera

00:06:25.660 --> 00:06:27.130
And I think that's the beauty of it.

00:06:27.360 --> 00:06:32.680
I also think that's why so many youtubers come and go-they forget about this part. A-and that's fine.

00:06:32.680 --> 00:06:38.680
Y'know, it's not like everything has to be super personal and everything has to be so, 'Oh, I love you guys so much

00:06:38.680 --> 00:06:40.100
You're my family.'

00:06:40.280 --> 00:06:43.040
Youtube... is... a hobby and a job

00:06:43.220 --> 00:06:46.540
at the same time, which can be really hard to balance.

00:06:46.900 --> 00:06:51.700
I think a lot of people don't realize this, but, you get to set your own hours, you get to set your own pace.

00:06:51.979 --> 00:06:59.299
But it basically means you'll be working 24/7 like it's really hard to turn off youtube in your brain. I'm always checking videos

00:06:59.300 --> 00:07:03.770
How are they doing? I'm always checking stats. I'm always checking comments

00:07:03.900 --> 00:07:08.640
What are people saying? What are people thinking? And it's really hard to turn off

00:07:08.640 --> 00:07:13.680
It's not like a nine-to-five job you go in you do your job, okay, now I'm done. Phew, I can relax.

00:07:14.320 --> 00:07:19.880
I-I really struggle a lot with this, an-and just trying to shut my brain off and 'Okay now I'm doing this, now

00:07:19.880 --> 00:07:25.340
I'm doing that.' And that's why I really enjoy having an office, because I-I can do my work here

00:07:25.340 --> 00:07:28.360
And then once I'm back home, I can just relax.

00:07:28.840 --> 00:07:34.900
Eh-I-It's... I-I guess my advice here is to try and separate it. I treat YouTube with a-with a lot of respect

00:07:35.940 --> 00:07:42.120
Because I feel so lucky to be in the situation that I am. I think a lot of youtubers take- take uh...

00:07:42.180 --> 00:07:43.470
YouTube very...

00:07:43.470 --> 00:07:47.839
Casually. I'll just upload a video. I need some money. I'll upload a video

00:07:48.620 --> 00:07:52.280
May-maybe I'm a little naive for saying that but, I-I always get the question

00:07:53.060 --> 00:07:57.420
'What happens if you miss a day, Felix? What's the big deal? Who's gonna care?'

00:07:57.460 --> 00:08:02.500
Wh-who-It's okay. You don't have to upload all the time, but it's like I set the schedule for me

00:08:02.500 --> 00:08:10.480
I know I can do it, it is my job to do it still. I have to do it, okay? I-I see Youtube as a...

00:08:12.380 --> 00:08:15.980
It's not going to last forever, but I might as well make the most of it...meanwhile.

00:08:16.760 --> 00:08:21.440
every YouTuber has-has a-has a life span.

00:08:21.540 --> 00:08:28.280
Market yourself. Most youtubers that you are watching got a helping hand to get where they are. Maybe they don't admit it

00:08:28.980 --> 00:08:34.220
Maybe I'm just wrong. Most youtubers had some helping hand. Maybe th-
maybe they uh...

00:08:34.340 --> 00:08:39.700
Maybe their videos were posted on a website y'know? That prom-that thought okay, 'This is a cool video...'

00:08:39.860 --> 00:08:46.160
Maybe you got trending on reddit, y'know? Maybe your family member was the youtuber or maybe a friend of you-o-of

00:08:46.200 --> 00:08:50.580
Of that person was a youtuber they helped them. Getting that helping hand on YouTube

00:08:50.589 --> 00:08:51.339
It's not essential

00:08:51.339 --> 00:08:52.130
but it's-it

00:08:52.130 --> 00:08:59.349
makes YouTube easy mode pretty much. To already... the hardest part of Youtube is to establish your very first audience. If you can get

00:08:59.350 --> 00:09:02.020
hat for free from someone else, hell, yeah!

00:09:02.860 --> 00:09:06.120
Hell yeah, that's the best! But a lot- I see a lot of

00:09:06.420 --> 00:09:12.320
misunderstanding of this as well, because, for example, I did the shout out competition in the past and, uh...

00:09:12.320 --> 00:09:17.320
For example Jack was one of them, Ken was one of them. And a lot of people look at them and be like, 'Oh

00:09:17.360 --> 00:09:24.160
Oh, you got a shout out from Pewdiepie. Aww, aww that's so bullshit. If I had one, I would be big.' Fuck you.

00:09:24.380 --> 00:09:28.640
No, i-that's not how it works. A shout out can only get you so far.

00:09:28.780 --> 00:09:36.420
I-I-It gets you that-that bass audience, maybe, but they're not going to stay unless you're worthwhile staying to - they're not going to care about

00:09:36.460 --> 00:09:41.860
watching any more videos, unless you upload videos - unless you upload videos that people care about.

00:09:41.860 --> 00:09:46.040
You don't need a shout out, and a shout out isn't necessarily going to help you,

00:09:46.160 --> 00:09:49.140
Unless your content is interesting. That's just how it is.

00:09:49.660 --> 00:09:54.940
You see people all the time in my comment section marketing their own YouTube channel. I find it...

00:09:54.980 --> 00:10:02.020
very disrespectful to do that. It annoys the hell out of me. 'Cuz it's basically just ignoring what I worked on...

00:10:02.440 --> 00:10:04.520
and basically just saying, 'Hey look at me!'

00:10:04.900 --> 00:10:10.240
I do think you should market yourself somehow if you really care about growing your channel.

00:10:10.240 --> 00:10:13.400
Now, I don't know what the best method is, but everyone has a secret

00:10:13.540 --> 00:10:19.180
I'm sure of how they try to get their channel out there. Maybe something they're ashamed of that they wouldn't admit.

00:10:19.180 --> 00:10:27.240
I-I think most youtubers have it. I, for example, used to find commenters on-on videos similar to mine and uh...

00:10:27.280 --> 00:10:33.200
I would write a private message to them being like, 'Hey! I see that you enjoyed this channel. Maybe you will enjoy mine!'

00:10:33.820 --> 00:10:37.440
I know. Extremely embarrassing, extremely pathetic, but I used to do it.

00:10:37.660 --> 00:10:42.340
A least it's not intrusive on someone else's work, okay? So, I-if y...

00:10:42.340 --> 00:10:48.160
I recommend marketing yourself somehow, I just d-don't- a-and it's nothing shameful about doing it,

00:10:48.160 --> 00:10:51.020
But don't be fucking obnoxious and disrespectful doing it,

00:10:51.040 --> 00:10:53.100
That-tha-that's my point with that.

00:10:53.100 --> 00:10:55.040
Next up is don't fucking trust anyone.

00:10:55.040 --> 00:10:57.140
Growing my channel on YouTube

00:10:57.140 --> 00:11:03.260
I've come across so many toxic people, people that just want your s-audience your subscribers

00:11:03.260 --> 00:11:04.060
Uh...

00:11:04.060 --> 00:11:06.600
They don't give a shit about you. They'll lie to you.

00:11:06.600 --> 00:11:07.800
Uhm....

00:11:07.800 --> 00:11:09.420
They'll try and manipulate you.

00:11:09.540 --> 00:11:14.620
I think I'm- one of my best skills as a human being, is to cut out toxic people.

00:11:14.620 --> 00:11:19.839
I have very little tolerance for people in general, and if I find them to be abusive or disrespectful,

00:11:20.180 --> 00:11:23.100
I have no problem with cutting out these people in my life.

00:11:23.540 --> 00:11:25.420
I know some people really struggle with this

00:11:26.100 --> 00:11:31.620
And I think as a youtuber you're just really gonna have to be cut and dry with people. It's just how it is.

00:11:32.440 --> 00:11:33.180
Networks.

00:11:33.420 --> 00:11:35.100
You may have heard of networks a lot

00:11:35.110 --> 00:11:41.830
I'm-I'm technically signed up with the network still, but I'm not planning to stay with the network. YouTube wouldn't sign

00:11:42.350 --> 00:11:48.279
with gaming channels. You could not monetize your videos if you were a gaming channel, back in the day

00:11:48.280 --> 00:11:50.040
It was the worst thing

00:11:50.040 --> 00:11:56.660
I think that could possibly happen to the gaming community on YouTube because essentially networks got so much power,

00:11:56.920 --> 00:11:58.480
Because we were obligated,

00:11:58.800 --> 00:11:59.960
to sign with them.

00:12:00.400 --> 00:12:06.620
So basically, as a gamer, you would get these insanely bad deals with networks where they would give you half of your revenue

00:12:06.940 --> 00:12:07.440
and

00:12:07.440 --> 00:12:09.340
Give you, essentially,

00:12:09.340 --> 00:12:11.680
nothing back. Networks still take a...

00:12:11.720 --> 00:12:17.540
Huge portion of your revenue if you're a small Youtuber. I still get a lot of people asking me, 'Hey, I'm a youtuber,

00:12:17.580 --> 00:12:19.080
I-should I sign up to the network?'

00:12:20.660 --> 00:12:25.140
'I don't know blah blah blah,' or 'do they increase my CPM blah blah blah...' Most likely they don't

00:12:25.160 --> 00:12:25.900
Uh...

00:12:25.980 --> 00:12:28.980
From my experience, they don't sell ads on your videos

00:12:29.180 --> 00:12:34.839
Think about most networks they have- like what, thousands of channels in them. Why would they care about your channel?

00:12:34.839 --> 00:12:35.470
Y'know?

00:12:35.470 --> 00:12:39.459
How are they going to focus on all these channels? It just doesn't make any sense.

00:12:39.670 --> 00:12:44.680
I would not recommend signing with the network if I was a smaller youtuber these days. That being said,

00:12:45.560 --> 00:12:47.560
Networks definitely helped me,

00:12:47.750 --> 00:12:49.750
to a certain degree,

00:12:49.880 --> 00:12:53.480
But I think as a smaller channel, it's completely useless.

00:12:53.480 --> 00:12:56.800
They're just going to take a portion of your revenue and give you nothing back

00:12:56.800 --> 00:12:59.380
You're not obligated to sign with a network anymore

00:12:59.540 --> 00:13:04.540
So, I would recommend against if you're a smaller channel. Which brings me to my next point:

00:13:04.540 --> 00:13:05.580
Get a lawyer.

00:13:05.580 --> 00:13:06.700
Don't sign anything

00:13:07.380 --> 00:13:09.620
without professional, over-a-a

00:13:09.760 --> 00:13:11.820
A professional overlooking what you're doing?

00:13:11.860 --> 00:13:19.380
I signed contract that were- that led me into month-long processes of trying to get out of those contracts. I-It's a lot cheaper

00:13:19.480 --> 00:13:24.840
To have a lawyer look over the contract and knowing exactly what you're getting yourself, into than

00:13:25.220 --> 00:13:29.160
Afterwards, gettin' a lawyer to try and get you out of this situation.

00:13:29.160 --> 00:13:34.900
Get a lawyer and get an accountant if you're-s- if you're making money off YouTube, and do it early.

00:13:35.360 --> 00:13:38.139
I think setting those two things up earlier is better than later.

00:13:38.540 --> 00:13:42.720
I realize this is a lot of information, but I think I saw this as a sort of...

00:13:43.660 --> 00:13:45.380
Me talking to myself in the past,

00:13:46.240 --> 00:13:46.740
Uh...

00:13:46.820 --> 00:13:48.920
And the sort of stuff that I learned through these uh,

00:13:48.940 --> 00:13:54.480
years of making videos on YouTube. And I try to keep it as, uh, actual advice and constructive as possible,

00:13:54.900 --> 00:13:55.400
But

00:13:55.540 --> 00:13:56.740
I would like to finish with...

00:13:58.780 --> 00:14:00.360
Make Youtube with the right intention.

00:14:00.500 --> 00:14:06.140
I see so many people wanting to make y-youtube videos because they want to get famous, they want to make money

00:14:06.320 --> 00:14:06.820
Uh...

00:14:06.820 --> 00:14:10.900
which is all great stuff. And YouTube really is an amazing place for it- for that, but,

00:14:12.040 --> 00:14:13.560
make YouTube videos,

00:14:13.579 --> 00:14:18.759
because you enjoy making them. If you don't enjoy making them, you're not going to keep making them

00:14:18.820 --> 00:14:20.860
You're g- just going to fall off at some point

00:14:21.300 --> 00:14:21.940
And

00:14:21.940 --> 00:14:27.680
you're going to get frustrated that, uh, it didn't turn out the way you wanted it to be. If you make videos

00:14:27.680 --> 00:14:30.420
that you enjoy making 'em, then you can't lose.

00:14:31.180 --> 00:14:37.440
It doesn't matter if you don't get a lot of subscribers. If- like I was equally happy, when I had a couple hundred subscribers.

00:14:37.940 --> 00:14:44.300
I thought that was the equally fun just to have some people watching them. If you make videos that you enjoy making,

00:14:44.740 --> 00:14:46.620
other people will enjoy watching them.

00:14:46.620 --> 00:14:53.660
I really, really strongly believe in that. So if you're not enjoying making videos, then don't make videos.

00:14:54.160 --> 00:14:54.860
(laughs)

00:14:55.220 --> 00:14:56.880
I hope this was helpful.

00:14:56.880 --> 00:14:59.700
I'm not-I'm not sure, to be honest, if it was.

00:15:00.020 --> 00:15:00.520
Uh...

00:15:00.580 --> 00:15:04.740
But I hope i-it was interesting at least, I don't know, I don't know, here you go.

00:15:04.959 --> 00:15:07.220
I did the video finally.

00:15:07.220 --> 00:15:08.320
Leave a like my sister fisters...

00:15:09.280 --> 00:15:10.980
and stay, sfisterin'!

